  "clipping_analysis_statement": {
    "preserved_finding": "66/66 bit errors co-located with spatial blocks undergoing dynamic range clipping (x < 0 or x > 255)",
    "causality_distinction": "Co-location demonstrates strong spatial correlation on high-contrast DIV2K carriers, but does not constitute causal proof. Confounding local frequency characteristics in edge blocks contribute to both clipping and larger coefficient distortions. Furthermore, at the zero-margin boundary (Delta_rec = 0.0), spatial rounding noise alone can cause bit flips even in unclipped blocks."
